{#-
  Base document shell: head, skip link, header, page content, footer (on
  every page, project lead 2026-11-07).
  Child layouts (page, info, topics, urgent) provide <main id="main">.

  Front matter read here:
    title       page title, used alone as the <title> (no site name; a
                page without one falls back to site.siteName)
    summary     meta description
    page_id     rendered as <body data-page-id> (SPEC §7, §13)
    page_width  "medium" (1280px) or "wide" (1360px); default 1200px
    styles      extra stylesheets under src/css/, e.g. ["pages/help.css"]
    scripts     extra ES modules in src/js/, e.g. ["players.js"], loaded in
                <head> with type="module" (deferred, so they never block
                rendering). The moduleScripts filter (eleventy.config.js)
                adds events.js first, when features.events is on, on pages
                that track page views or load players.js or search.js, and
                drops stats-switch.js while it is off, and rating.js while
                features.ratings is off (SPEC §10.1, §11, §12)
    track_page_view  true on the pages that send a page_view (SPEC §10.2):
                problem pages, Start here and Getting urgent help. Rendered
                as <body data-page-view> whatever the feature switches say:
                events.js sends a page_view where it finds it, and pages.json
                (SPEC §8.3) reads it to tell the Worker which pages may send
                one
    header      "minimal" for the logo-and-back-link header (urgent help)
    referrer    a referrer policy for this page alone, as a meta tag; the
                search page uses "strict-origin" so its ?q= never travels on
                (SPEC §8.1)

  The feedback dialog (SPEC §13): on every page with a page_id, while
  features.feedback is exactly true, the dialog follows the footer (outside
  it and outside <main>) and feedback.js loads last in <head>. The 404 page
  (no page_id) keeps the plain link to the Contact page, as does any page
  without JavaScript.
-#}
{%- set feedbackDialog = site.features.feedback === true and page_id -%}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-AU">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>{{ title or site.siteName }}</title>
  {%- if referrer %}
  <meta name="referrer" content="{{ referrer }}">
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if summary %}
  <meta name="description" content="{{ summary }}">
  {%- endif %}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/tokens.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/site.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/components.css">
  {%- for href in styles | stylesheets %}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ href }}">
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- if header != 'minimal' %}
  <script type="module" src="/js/menu.js"></script>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- for src in scripts | moduleScripts({ features: site.features, track: track_page_view }) %}
  <script type="module" src="{{ src }}"></script>
  {%- endfor %}
  {%- if feedbackDialog %}
  <script type="module" src="/js/feedback.js"></script>
  {%- endif %}
</head>
<body{% if page_width %} class="page--{{ page_width }}"{% endif %}{% if page_id %} data-page-id="{{ page_id }}"{% endif %}{% if track_page_view %} data-page-view{% endif %}>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  {% if header == 'minimal' %}{% include "partials/minimal-header.njk" %}{% else %}{% include "partials/site-header.njk" %}{% endif %}
  {{ content | safe }}
  {% include "partials/site-footer.njk" %}
  {%- if feedbackDialog %}
  {% include "partials/feedback-dialog.njk" %}
  {%- endif %}
</body>
</html>
